# Environment configuration for the Tango KYC Verification backend.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local tooling and to
# `supabase/functions/.env` for the local Edge Function runtime, then fill in
# the values. NEVER commit the real `.env` files: only `.env.example` is tracked.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where each value comes from
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#   For the local stack, run:  supabase status -o env
#   The ANON key is public and is also placed in the Flutter build.
#   The SERVICE_ROLE key is a full-access secret: backend only, never Flutter.
#
# EMAIL_API_KEY
#   Resend Dashboard -> API Keys -> Create API Key
#   https://resend.com/api-keys
#   Free tier: 3,000 emails/month, 100/day. Backend only.
#   INBOUND ONLY: this key is still used to fetch the body of a received reply.
#   Outbound mail is sent through Mailjet (see MAILJET_* below).
#
# EMAIL_FROM
#   The Resend-side sender. With no custom domain, Resend's free tier only
#   allows `onboarding@resend.dev`, and it can only send to the account owner
#   address. Verify a domain at https://resend.com/domains to send to any address.
#   Outbound mail no longer uses this value; MAILJET_FROM_EMAIL replaces it.
#
# EMAIL_INBOUND_DOMAIN / EMAIL_INBOUND_MAILBOX
#   The domain configured for inbound mail at https://resend.com/domains with
#   receiving enabled. Replies go to: <mailbox>+<reply_token>@<domain>
#   The `+<reply_token>` suffix is what lets the backend identify the ticket.
#   Unchanged by the Mailjet switch: Mailjet sends the mail, but the Reply-To
#   still points here so replies keep reaching Resend Inbound.
#
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   Resend Dashboard -> Webhooks -> (your webhook) -> Signing Secret
#   Starts with `whsec_`. Used to verify every inbound webhook.
#
# MAILJET_API_KEY / MAILJET_SECRET_KEY
#   Mailjet Dashboard -> Account -> API Key Management (Master API Key, or a
#   dedicated Send-only key): https://app.mailjet.com/account/apikeys
#   The API key is the HTTP Basic username, the secret key the password.
#   Backend only: never expose either to Flutter.
#
# MAILJET_FROM_EMAIL
#   The validated sender used for OUTBOUND mail, e.g.
#   `Tango KYC Verification <kyc@yourdomain.com>`.
#   Validate it at https://app.mailjet.com/account/sender
#   Mailjet rejects any From address that is not a validated sender, so this
#   value has no default and outbound sending stays disabled until it is set.
#
# ADMIN_EMAIL
#   The support mailbox that receives new requests and replies to them.

# --- Supabase -------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Email: outbound (Mailjet) --------------------------------------------
MAILJET_API_KEY=
MAILJET_SECRET_KEY=
MAILJET_FROM_EMAIL=

# --- Email: inbound (Resend) ----------------------------------------------
EMAIL_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=Tango KYC Verification <onboarding@resend.dev>
EMAIL_INBOUND_DOMAIN=
EMAIL_INBOUND_MAILBOX=reply
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Application ----------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_EMAIL=rasonjonathan6@gmail.com

# Anti-spam limits are NOT environment variables: they live in the `rate_limit`
# row of the `app_settings` table and are edited with SQL. See
# docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md for the exact statements.
